atlas commands-project-node

architecture mcp-project-native-owner
  canonical_name McpProjectNativeOwner
  family commands
  domain MCP / Local project and native operation owner
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Can the complete local project MCP surface run without Python while preserving its local checkout, native stores, approval gates and durable receipt boundaries?
  purpose Replace the launchd Python project node with one Bun transport and bounded semantic owners for project reads, operator mutations, composed native operations and the shared Spines surface; configured HTTPS placement changes execution location without substituting the project checkout or inventing another evaluator.
  node_types ProjectTool
  node_types PatchReceipt
  node_types GenerationReceipt
  state_types admitted
  state_types refused
  state_types outcome_uncertain
  internal_calculus captured thirty-tool catalog -> structural argument validation -> exact owner table -> bounded subprocess or native store operation -> typed result and existing owner receipts
  invariant bearer authentication precedes body parsing or owner invocation; non-read-only operations serialize within the service and overload refuses rather than creating an unbounded queue
  invariant subprocess argv is never interpolated into a local shell; timeout and output overflow terminate the process group and cannot be returned as truncated success
  invariant project reads stay beneath the configured local checkout; search arguments cannot select ripgrep options, and Git reads disable external diff, textconv and fsmonitor helpers
  invariant project_read accepts one range or at most sixteen related file ranges, with whole-file SHA-256 and conditional content omission; batches share 32 MiB source and 512 KiB result limits and never claim an atomic multi-file snapshot
  invariant native discovery can filter and page capability summaries without executing binaries; family and capability manifests load once per request, and the next request reads fresh metadata
  invariant path-only patch preview reports exact preimages, touched-path dirty state and existing write constraints without creating operator state or conferring apply authority; patch validation and effect-time checks remain required
  invariant Atlas queries invoke the existing root-relative Bun query owner and retain its provenance instead of importing a retired Python module or independently reimplementing registry semantics
  invariant manual patches require the existing write gate and approval token; low-risk patches retain configured path, size and dirty-file policy; postimage mismatch refuses rollback and commit
  invariant Python syntax execution is retired explicitly; Bun syntax parsing neither executes source nor claims type or runtime verification
  invariant cloudflare-bridge verification builds the existing native queue and runs a fixed local fixture suite; arbitrary paths and targets refuse, and build or test failure remains failure
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_operator.test.mjs verifies fixed bridge scope, build-before-test ordering and failure propagation
  interacts project-mcp-verifies-cloudflare-bridge
  invariant native inventory and invocation inspect executable format without executing candidates and refuse interpreter launchers rather than preserving hidden Python execution through a native-looking filename
  invariant Matrix has only its configured local or remote native store; an absent configuration refuses without creating a substitute database
  invariant ForeignTwin observation and native invocation share BONFYRE_FOREIGN_ROOT, defaulting to the existing local MCP foreign store; configured absolute or home-relative roots are honored for both receipts and retained bodies, and cwd-relative roots refuse
  forbidden_inference an authenticated tool invocation or available native binary -> institutional, payment, publication, foreign or delegation authority
  forbidden_inference byte-level patch checks -> atomic exclusion of external writers or proof of semantic correctness
  forbidden_inference passing fixtures or a constructible Bun server -> a deployed replacement or complete retirement of other Python services
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_catalog.json
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_node.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/control_plane_app_build.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/control_plane_app_resource.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_runtime.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_reads.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_operator.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_native.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_spines.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/tests/project_workflow_benchmark.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_owner.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_v6.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_fabric.mjs
  source_path deploy/launchd/project_mcp_cutover.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_node.test.mjs covers thirty original routes, twenty-nine shared Spines routes and eighteen V6 routes, resource and prompt bindings, authentication and structural refusal
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_spines.test.mjs composes the real Spines/Wasm owner through a simulated HTTPS transport; preserves write/STOP gates and requires an explicitly scoped remote credential
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_v6.test.mjs dedicated remote credentials, fixed endpoint, exact owner catalog, pre-dispatch write and STOP refusal
  witness packs/no-simulation/mcp-workflow-20261017/project-fabric-live.json records the October 17 eighty-six-tool live catalogue, exact five-operation delivery schemas and authenticated Project-to-Fabric reads after scoped service reloads; all Fabric durable tables, receipts and STOP controls are unchanged
  known_gap the live delivery witness exercises status and receipt reads, not every composed operation or a paid model mission; V6 Python mission compilation still needs native replacement
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_reads.test.mjs covers real Git status/diff, root confinement, option injection, bounded tree/read and the existing Atlas owner
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_node.test.mjs exercises batched and conditional source reads and nonmutating path preflight over authenticated loopback HTTP through the existing tools
  witness packs/no-simulation/mcp-workflow-20261017/measurement.json records local HTTP result bytes for full, paginated and targeted inventory, eight-file batched reads and unchanged refreshes; timings are single current-implementation observations, not before-and-after remote latency evidence
  witness packs/no-simulation/mcp-workflow-20261017/live-readback.json records the scoped October 17 project-service reload and authenticated readback of filtered discovery, batch reads, conditional refresh and path preflight with unchanged configuration and operator STOP state
  witness packs/no-simulation/mcp-workflow-20261017/chatgpt-connector-readback.json verifies authenticated current-source reads through the ChatGPT app; its earlier schemas still strip inventory filters and refuse batched reads
  witness packs/no-simulation/mcp-workflow-20261017/app-refresh-readback.json records successful filtered inventory, two-file batch reads, conditional unchanged reads and path-only preflight through the refreshed ChatGPT app on October 17
  witness packs/no-simulation/mcp-workflow-20261017/app-relay-readback.json records all five delivery tools exposed in the refreshed app and successful app calls for Fabric status, compact task status and receipt discovery; operator admission remains paused with no active or queued tasks
  known_gap app delivery discovery and read routes are verified, while submission through guarded apply is covered by real HTTP fixtures with injected agents; no live model quality or production task execution is claimed
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_operator.test.mjs covers isolated patch and SQLite operator state transitions without live mutations
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_operator.test.mjs verifies mode-change rollback refusal against recorded postimage modes under umask 077 and 022
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_node.test.mjs builds and serves the SDK dependency-inclusive control-plane bundle through the authenticated resource path within the 512 KiB limit; 2026-10-23 operator and node suites pass 26 tests
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_native.test.mjs covers native format admission, configured Matrix coordinates and composed generation/fulfillment owner receipts with offline fixtures
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_native.test.mjs exercises observation followed by native lookup with both default and explicit ForeignTwin roots, verifies retained body bytes and refuses cwd-dependent roots
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_native.test.mjs executes the compiled BonfyreProject owner against a retained receipt through the same MCP invocation path, beyond the mocked transport checks
  witness 2026-10-07 live native MCP observation 635f56ae-653d-4181-bc47-c375efe050de retained the RED3 Acrylic Shirt Display Easel page; resolution ed973250-2420-4d38-b64f-5c21abdb463c found that full HTTP-200 observation in the configured store with matching digest 3164c2a35518262c5d0b132f71d424ee2906a70fb4ee67b50ba6698ec7425981; project cl:red3-product-pages retains the receipt reference
  forbidden_inference agreement between observation and lookup roots -> complete source coverage, public visibility or rights to act against the observed client
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_runtime.test.mjs covers literal argv, timeout, output overflow, strict decoding and retired-interpreter refusal
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_transport_adversarial.test.mjs covers malformed request identity, credential redaction, concurrency limits and timeout cleanup of a SIGTERM-resistant grandchild
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_live_witness.mjs verifies real HTTP authentication, all thirty catalog names, five resources, two templates, four prompts and concrete local read owners without operator effects
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_node_cutover.json records the 2026-10-02 launchd promotion, old Python PID exit, unchanged non-program configuration and live Bun HTTP witness
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_node_read_benchmark.json records twenty-five alternating warmed HTTP samples per owner with bounded-read parity and scoped latency gains; it is not a system-wide scaling measurement
  known_gap portable filesystem confinement is not openat2-style exclusion of a hostile process swapping ancestor directories during an operation; the checkout and configured owner roots remain trusted local state
  invariant a generation projection attempt is retained as outcome_uncertain before invoking a native owner; matching pending or failed receipts inside the bounded retry lookup prohibit automatic replay and preserve generated output for reconciliation
  known_gap exotic rename, copy, deletion, mode-changing, binary and symlink patches refuse; legacy patch receipts lacking mode evidence cannot be automatically reverted
  known_gap the installed Bun owner's real model generation, downstream native projections and configured remote Matrix route have not been exercised by this cutover witness
  known_gap facilitator decimal or exponent numeric tokens refuse rather than claiming Python JSON digest equivalence without a lossless numeric representation
  known_gap generation retry lookup currently covers at most 512 directory entries and one hour; it is a bounded local recovery aid, not global idempotency or an exactly-once guarantee
  known_gap receipt replacement is atomic for process-level failure recovery but does not fsync file and directory metadata for sudden-power-loss durability

interaction recursive-mcp-uses-local-project-owner
  source mcp-recursive-native-overlay
  destination mcp-project-native-owner
  relation exact-local-owner-rpc
  preserves authenticated project tool schemas, local checkout identity, native-store coordinates, approval gates and returned receipts
  drops any implication that the remote overlay checkout is the local project or that listing a tool grants effect authority
  forbidden_inference a remote gateway tool listing -> a reachable, authorized or successfully executed local owner
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_overlay.test.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/recursive_overlay.cue
  binding integrations/mcp/project_node.mjs

interaction project-node-uses-delivery-fabric
  source mcp-project-native-owner
  destination dual-agent-fabric-native-owner
  relation exact-catalog-bound-delivery-rpc
  preserves five existing operation names and schemas, durable task and receipt identity, Project write admission, Fabric STOP and queue policy, source snapshot coverage and effect-time Project patch checks
  drops duplicated task stores, automatic resume, automatic retries after uncertain effects and caller-selected endpoints
  forbidden_inference an advertised implementation relay -> provider authorization, an accepting broker, successful implementation or permission to apply
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_fabric.test.mjs verifies fixed placement, dedicated remote credentials, pre-dispatch write and STOP gates, cancellation while stopped, schema validation and propagated uncertain errors
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/fabric_project_workflow.test.mjs exercises real HTTP from Project to Fabric and back to Project apply, real Git isolation and Bun tests with deterministic agents
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/oauth_institution_slice_test.sh refuses delivery reads and effects for personal and institution sessions and preserves the existing administrative upstream
  binding integrations/mcp/project_fabric.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/project_owner.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/project_node.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/bonfyre_oauth_gateway.mjs

interaction project-node-uses-bounded-atlas
  source mcp-project-native-owner
  destination atlas-context-provider
  relation shared-root-relative-query
  preserves operation, identifier or query, bounded answer and index provenance
  drops full registry serialization and independent transport-side Atlas semantics
  forbidden_inference a returned Atlas projection -> canonical truth independent of its provenance
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_reads.test.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/project_reads.mjs
  binding architecture/atlas-query.mjs

interaction project-generation-names-proof-owners
  source mcp-project-native-owner
  destination mcp-generation-proof
  relation receipted-native-projection
  preserves local completion digest and exact CMS, ArtifactGraph, Flow and DisCIPL owner coordinates
  drops any inference that generation, a stored row or a defined WorkGraph enacts an external effect
  forbidden_inference a returned generation receipt -> independent verification of every referenced owner projection
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_native.test.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/project_native.mjs
  invariant the OAuth gateway issues the BonfyreAuth session as the access token with expires_in equal to the session's remaining lifetime (from http-login expires_at) and a sealed refresh token (AES-256-GCM, key derived from the seal secret or the project token file, no server state); a refresh_token grant is honoured only while bonfyre-auth verify still accepts the session and the client_id matches, so logout, expiry or a disabled account ends it
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/oauth_institution_slice_test.sh runs the full authorization-code flow with PKCE against a fixture BonfyreAuth: expires_in beyond one day, refresh returns the live session, tampered or other-client refresh tokens and a logged-out session are refused (2026-10-17)
  witness packs/no-simulation/mcp-timing-20261017/findings.md: before the refresh grant, ChatGPT tool calls stalled 13-24 minutes on authentication retry because the gateway declared an 8-hour token with no refresh token while sessions lasted 7 days
  forbidden_inference a refresh token -> standing authority; it is the session sealed, and dies with the session
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_products.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/tests/project_products.test.mjs
  invariant the products owner exposes books_learn, books_profiles, books_book, monitor_mentions and manifest_lot: the bank export, watch and listing text travel in the call, the product modules decide, learned books are named profiles kept 0600 under ~/.bonfyre/estate-local/books; every operation but books_learn is declared read-only, and a local model that cannot be admitted is reported, not hidden
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_products.test.mjs proves profile learn/list/book with an unread amount held and the model unavailable reported, path-like profile names and undeclared arguments refused, an empty archive answered without a model, and a manifest that needs the model refused with the reason (2026-10-17); over live :3051, books_learn on 6,000 lines took 810 ms and books_book on 1,500 lines 568 ms
  forbidden_inference a booked line returned to a chat -> a posted ledger entry; books_book posts nothing
  known_gap a books profile belongs to this machine, not to a client organisation; ChatGPT sees new operations only after its cached tool list is refreshed

architecture project-spines-distributed-binding
  canonical_name ProjectSpinesDistributedBinding
  family commands
  domain Execution / Authenticated owner federation
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Can the same temporal, reduction and placement operations be reached across an authenticated machine boundary without copying their semantics or exporting general credentials?
  internal_calculus original Spines catalog -> Project operation table -> fixed local or HTTPS owner -> original operation and receipt
  invariant all twenty-nine schemas and operation identities derive from one Spines catalog; caller arguments cannot choose the endpoint or executable
  invariant proof-writing reads require write admission, operator STOP remains authoritative, and HTTPS requires a separately configured owner credential
  invariant public, self and institution apertures do not inherit administrative Spines operations
  forbidden_inference simulated HTTPS or a portable Wasm module -> deployed multi-host execution, tenant-safe scheduling or production scaling
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_spines.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/owned_mcp_client.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/bonfyre_oauth_gateway.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_spines.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/oauth_institution_slice_test.sh actual gateway fixture refuses self/institution reduction with zero upstream calls and forwards an admitted administrative reduction once
  known_gap public mcp.aurekai.work metadata observed on 2026-10-03 exposes the read-only estate aperture with no authorization server, not the declared protected gateway; no two-host execution is inferred
  known_gap remote operation responses are authenticated transport evidence, not hardware attestation or independent correctness verification

interaction project-spines-reuses-semantic-owner
  source project-spines-distributed-binding
  destination native-spines-bun-owner
  relation authenticated-location-independent-owner-call
  preserves operation schemas, bounded execution, owner receipts, candidate classification and effect refusal
  drops duplicated remote algorithms and an assumption that placement grants authority
  forbidden_inference a selected remote endpoint -> authorization to disclose arbitrary tenant data or commit effects
  binding integrations/mcp/project_spines.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_spines.test.mjs
